+We develop DGF to recover damped oscillations from noisy observations with a known gap. The time--frequency branch uses complex Morlet continuous wavelet transform (CWT) features, including a second bank with explicit low-frequency coverage. The temporal branch preserves the sign and multiscale structure of the waveform. Mixing layers combine these complementary features, and sequence blocks connect context on both sides of the interval before a decoder synthesizes the clean waveform. Related time-series models use temporal and feature mixing to combine information across scales~\cite{TSMixer2023,TimeMixer2024}. Whitening uses a calibrated power spectral density (PSD), while mask-aware and joint-channel modules refine the decoded waveform. A coefficient head adjusts a training-derived signal basis using observation-derived noise and phase features. A multiscale convolutional module then reconstructs residual structure in physical coordinates, with supervision that follows the decaying envelope.
 
 The observation model is $d=Gh+n$: $G$ suppresses the signal over one interval, and noise is present throughout the record. We report reconstruction accuracy for $\rho\ge10$ alongside the complete test population, and examine recovery across intervals containing the signal-envelope peak.
 
